sis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: We set ${v}_{2}={a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 3**. Next, we find ${v}_{3}$ using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{3}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{8}{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{5}{10}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{b}=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(\\frac{3}{2})}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-95846" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "385791cbbb2c007e60753451a219f151690c457248eec4cb564bdac41082b892"} {"ques