{2},{a}_{3}$ of the matrix $A,$ and an **orthonormal** basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ shown above. Given that ${a}_{1}⊥{a}_{2},$ and that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $|\\,c\\,|?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-40817" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the first two vectors are already orthogonal, we proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: We set ${v}_{2}={a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 3**. Next, we find ${v}_{3}$ using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{3}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-(-\\frac{16}{16})[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-(-\\frac{6}{6})[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize ${v}_{3}$ dividing it by $‖{v}_{3}‖=3\\sqrt{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{3} & =\\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖}=\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $|\\,c\\,|=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-40817" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "385791cbbb2c007e60753451a219f151690c457248eec4cb564bdac41082b892"} {"question" "q-40817" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-40817" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-40817" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-41626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c \\\\ d\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V=\\text{Col}(A)$ spanned by the columns ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ of the matrix $A$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ shown above. Given that ${a}_{1}⊥{a}_{2},$ and that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-41626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the first two vectors are already orthogonal, we proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: We set ${v}_{2}={a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 3**. Next, we find ${v}_{3}$ using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{3}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{4}{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{6}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{3}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(5[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-5[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{(-\\frac{2}{5})}{(-\\frac{1}{5})}=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-41626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "385791cbbb2c007e60753451a219f151690c457248eec4cb564bdac41082b892"} {"question" "q-41626" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-41626" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-41626" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-40772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c \\\\ d\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V=\\text{Col}(A)$ spanned by the columns ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ of the matrix $A$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ shown above. Given that ${a}_{1}⊥{a}_{2},$ and that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{a}{d}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-40772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the first two vectors are already orthogonal, we proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: We set ${v}_{2}={a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 3**. Next, we find ${v}_{3}$ using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{3}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-(-\\frac{6}{4})[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{2}{12}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{3}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(6[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+9[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{d}=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{3})}{(-\\frac{2}{3})}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-40772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "385791cbbb2c007e60753451a219f151690c457248eec4cb564bdac41082b892"} {"question" "q-40772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-40772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-40772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-140895" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {v}_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\\,,[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {v}_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\\,,[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c \\\\ d\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V=\\text{Col}(A)$ spanned by the columns ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ of the matrix $A,$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ shown above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-140895" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We proceed to find an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows:\n\n**Step 1.** We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2.** We find the vector ${v}_{2}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1}}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{22}{11}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** We find the vector ${v}_{3}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{11}{11}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{7}{7}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{c}=\\frac{3}{1}=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-140895" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "385791cbbb2c007e60753451a219f151690c457248eec4cb564bdac41082b892"} {"question" "q-140895" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-140895" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-140895" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-95862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {v}_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\\,,[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {v}_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\\,,[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c \\\\ d\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V=\\text{Col}(A)$ spanned by the columns ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ of the matrix $A,$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ shown above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-95862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We proceed to find an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows:\n\n**Step 1.** We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2.** We find the vector ${v}_{2}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1}}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{6}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** We find the vector ${v}_{3}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{6}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{12}{12}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{(-1)}{(-2)}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-95862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "385791cbbb2c007e60753451a219f151690c457248eec4cb564bdac41082b892"} {"question" "q-95862" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-95862" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-95862" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-40818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}],\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {v}_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\\,,[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {v}_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\\,,[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nSuppose that $V=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ Given that $B$ is an orthogonal basis for $V,$ and that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-40818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find an orthogonal basis $B$ of $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows:\n\n**Step 1.** We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2.** We find the vector ${v}_{2}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1}}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{10}{5}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** We find the vector ${v}_{3}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{15}{5}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{46}{46}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $\\frac{a}{b}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-40818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "385791cbbb2c007e60753451a219f151690c457248eec4cb564bdac41082b892"} {"question" "q-40818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-40818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-40818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-41631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {v}_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\\,,[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {v}_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\\,,[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c \\\\ d\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V=\\text{Col}(A)$ spanned by the columns ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ of the matrix $A,$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ shown above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{d}{a}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-41631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We proceed to find an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows:\n\n**Step 1.** We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2.** We find the vector ${v}_{2}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1}}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{2}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** We find the vector ${v}_{3}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{2}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{10}{20}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\frac{d}{a}=\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{2})}{(\\frac{1}{2})}=-3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-41631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "385791cbbb2c007e60753451a219f151690c457248eec4cb564bdac41082b892"} {"question" "q-41631" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-41631" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-41631" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-140826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {v}_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\\,,[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {v}_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\\,,[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nSuppose that $V=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ Given that $B$ is an orthogonal basis for $V,$ and that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-140826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find an orthogonal basis $B$ of $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows:\n\n**Step 1.** We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2.** We find the vector ${v}_{2}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1}}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** We find the vector ${v}_{3}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=-4,$ $b=-2,$ and $\\frac{a}{b}=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-140826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "385791cbbb2c007e60753451a219f151690c457248eec4cb564bdac41082b892"} {"question" "q-140826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-140826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "q-140826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5294c99f65717eba00191cf2df99292de6490d03a86efd1439270886b532e9a"} {"question" "e-5584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following vectors:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/assets/26a4907b9698a976361fbf6396c09a56edc417f177e512a82f6fb1495624f98b.png)\n\nSuppose that $V = \\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf a_1, \\mathbf a_2, \\mathbf a_3\\}.$ Given that $\\mathcal B = \\{\\mathbf a_1, \\mathbf a_2, \\mathbf b\\}$ is an orthogonal basis for $V, \\mathbf{a}_1 \\perp \\mathbf{a}_2,$ and that $\\mathcal B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\dfrac{c}{a}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/example-5584.json" "file_sha256" "2df00a764b1992ece68267cac9447cba8355a32ea64dc38f065efd4dee91e06a"} {"question" "e-5584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the first two vectors are already orthogonal, we proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: We set ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/assets/ea56a2ffc9a7f267e5de0cace94d505050e7df7ade72986b0b8e5ae6c91e7385.png)\n\n**Step 2**: We set ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/assets/a87589c86b41d3fd44e6346b300a103c16301bb6cde410084a794b5430b3599a.png)\n\n**Step 3**. Next, we find $\\mathbf{v}_3$ using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for $\\mathbf{v}_3$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-(-\\frac{2}{4})[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{0}{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-0[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=-\\dfrac 1 2,$ $c=-\\dfrac 3 2,$ and $\\dfrac{c}{a} = \\dfrac{\\left(-\\dfrac 3 2\\right)}{\\left(-\\dfrac 1 2\\right)} = 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/example-5584.json" "file_sha256" "2df00a764b1992ece68267cac9447cba8355a32ea64dc38f065efd4dee91e06a"} {"question" "e-8321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/assets/a0a83c2b8fe6a0ccf1e35f49f239e51c256ce3d19ddfe86ba9b215ddd1d3579b.png)\n\nConsider the subspace $V=\\textrm{Col}(A)$ spanned by the columns $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3$ of the matrix $A,$ and an **orthonormal** basis $\\mathcal{B}$ of $\\textrm{Col}(A),$ shown above. Given that $\\mathbf{a}_1 \\perp \\mathbf{a}_2,$ and that $\\mathcal B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $|\\,d\\,|?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/example-8321.json" "file_sha256" "06ec0796611c0c8bd524c2d1231961632930a39aff478e0b0cce8471cd833522"} {"question" "e-8321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the first two vectors are already orthogonal, we proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/assets/fac944c1f224d01dc33db95a5971ff47483e04ecf06492d8cfecb44d05de225c.png)\n\n**Step 2**: We set ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/assets/ce3195325db5c00042ec58cb51b8e17c77df742112ea7ad6481920647a6c77bb.png)\n\n**Step 3**. Next, we find $\\mathbf{v}_3$ using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for $\\mathbf{v}_3$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{10}{10}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{20}{20}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize $\\mathbf{v}_3$ dividing it by $\\|\\mathbf{v}_3\\| = \\sqrt{10}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{3} & =\\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $|\\,d\\,| = \\left|-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}\\right|=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/example-8321.json" "file_sha256" "06ec0796611c0c8bd524c2d1231961632930a39aff478e0b0cce8471cd833522"} {"question" "e-5585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/assets/1e6a41f2d6f834b7f9b8c937d19a4f47d45ee6bf2705d783e9a254e8478df15d.png)\n\nSuppose that $V = \\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf a_1, \\mathbf a_2, \\mathbf a_3\\}.$ Given that $\\mathcal B$ is an orthogonal basis for $V,$ and that $\\mathcal B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\dfrac{b}{c}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072057/example-5585.json" "file_sha256" "924dce093f9665e489b6f96de07a89639bab0f96954a0caf9119afd32421c922"} {"question" "e-5585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-soluti